{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787513055807,"sessionID":"ses_fcfec1ec3ffeTM9XJmOkxV2mTm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"functions.write:20","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-nnFPSx/checkout/benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/INCIDENT.md","content":"# Config-read incident\n\n## Summary\n\nOn 2026-08-23 the configuration endpoint for tenant `acme` returned `503 origin_timeout` for every request, even though an origin probe between requests showed the upstream was healthy.\n\n## User impact\n\nTenants could not fetch configuration for several minutes. Requests that should have recovered after the transient origin timeout continued to fail with the same timeout error, so the service stayed degraded longer than the actual outage.\n\n## Root cause and evidence\n\nThe cache stored the **promise** returned by the origin, not the eventual value. When the origin promise rejected, that rejected promise stayed in the cache map forever.\n\nCode evidence (`config-cache.mjs`):\n\n```js\nif (!pending) {\n  pending = Promise.resolve()\n    .then(() => loadFromOrigin(key))\n    .then(normalizeConfig);\n  entries.set(key, pending);   // ← rejected promise stored here\n}\n\nreturn copyConfig(await pending); // ← always re-awaiting the rejected promise\n}\n```\n\nAfter the first `ConfigOriginError`, `entries.get(\"acme\")` was still the rejected promise, so every subsequent `getConfig(\"acme\")` hit the cache and re-threw the same failure. The origin function was never called again.\n\nLog evidence (`incident.log`):\n\n```text\n2026-08-23T14:03:18.004Z ... cache=miss status=503 error=origin_timeout\n2026-08-23T14:03:18.407Z ... origin-probe ... status=200\n2026-08-23T14:03:19.015Z ... cache=hit status=503 error=origin_timeout\n2026-08-23T14:03:21.027Z ... cache=hit status=503 error=origin_timeout\n2026-08-23T14:03:21.031Z ... origin_load_count=1\n```\n\n`origin_load_count=1` confirms the cache never attempted a second origin call.\n\n## Why the logs were misleading\n\nThe `cache=hit` lines look like normal cache behavior, suggesting the cache is working and the problem must be upstream. The healthy origin probe also pointed away from the application. In reality the cache was \"hitting\" on a stored rejection, so `cache=hit` meant \"replaying the old failure\" rather than \"serving a cached success\". Without checking whether the cached value was a resolved or rejected promise, the logs sent the investigation toward the network instead of the caching logic.\n\n## Fix and regression coverage\n\nThe cache now deletes the failed entry only when the pending promise it created is still the current entry. This lets the next read retry the origin while preserving any replacement that was explicitly installed in the meantime.\n\nUpdated `config-cache.mjs`:\n\n```js\npending = Promise.resolve()\n  .then(() => loadFromOrigin(key))\n  .then(normalizeConfig)\n  .catch((error) => {\n    if (entries.get(key) === pending) {\n      entries.delete(key);\n    }\n    throw error;\n  });\n```\n\n`student-tests.mjs` now covers:\n\n1. A rejected load is removed and the next read retries the origin.\n2. A late failure of a replaced in-flight load does not evict the replacement.\n3. Concurrent callers on the same failing load all observe the same failure.\n4. An invalid origin result is evicted and does not poison future reads.\n5. Unrelated tenant failures do not evict successful entries.\n6. The API contract (503 + `retry-after: 1`, `no-store`, 200 recovery) is preserved.\n\n## Remaining risk\n\nEvery transient failure still incurs one origin load that fails for all waiting callers. There is no bounded retry or circuit breaker, so a truly unhealthy origin will be contacted on every new request for that tenant. A future improvement could add an exponential back-off for repeated origin errors, but that is out of scope for this incident.\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-nnFPSx/checkout/benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/INCIDENT.md","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/INCIDENT.md","time":{"start":1787513055800,"end":1787513055805}},"id":"prt_03014aa34001ivyJhJjvSRV01a","sessionID":"ses_fcfec1ec3ffeTM9XJmOkxV2mTm","messageID":"msg_0301491c90016XgMrTN7LelZ5h"}}
